## Tracing

`core/tracing.py`: every request and SQL query becomes an OpenTelemetry
span, sent to `OTEL_EXPORTER_ENDPOINT` over OTLP/HTTP. Empty, tracing is off.
With tracing on, JSON log lines also carry `trace_id` and `span_id`: from a
slow request's log line, search that trace ID in your tracing tool.

With a worker, a task's spans join the trace of the request that sent it
(taskiq's OpenTelemetry middleware carries the trace through the broker), and
the worker reports as `<app name> worker`.
